1
00:00:02,035 --> 00:00:03,275
GORDON: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,337 --> 00:00:06,017
LEE: What's your record for how
many banks you've robbed in one day?

3
00:00:07,841 --> 00:00:09,469
You're playing a
dangerous game, Lee.

4
00:00:09,543 --> 00:00:12,188
LEE: <i>My job is to make sure that
the people of The Narrows are safe.</i>

5
00:00:12,212 --> 00:00:14,511
<i>And I will do everything
in my power to ensure that.</i>

6
00:00:14,681 --> 00:00:15,825
GORDON: I'm
looking for Ed Nygma.

7
00:00:15,849 --> 00:00:17,818
Five banks were
robbed last night.

8
00:00:17,885 --> 00:00:19,820
Why don't you try going
after the real criminals?

9
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:21,297
<i>Making money off
the backs of the poor?</i>

10
00:00:21,321 --> 00:00:22,880
GORDON: <i>Like Gotham
Savings and Loan?</i>

11
00:00:22,990 --> 00:00:24,583
You are a fool!

12
00:00:24,691 --> 00:00:26,421
GORDON: Come out
with your hands up!

13
00:00:28,729 --> 00:00:30,106
I expected you
might come, Captain.

14
00:00:30,130 --> 00:00:31,130
There's two of them.

15
00:00:31,198 --> 00:00:32,375
HARVEY: <i>What if he's
nuttier than the other one?</i>

16
00:00:32,399 --> 00:00:33,610
JEREMIAH: <i>I'm
nothing like Jerome!</i>

17
00:00:33,634 --> 00:00:35,626
I'm gonna drive you mad.

18
00:00:35,836 --> 00:00:37,964
<i>But don't worry, all of
Gotham will be joining you.</i>

19
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:39,472
- GORDON: Hands up!
- Bombs away!

20
00:00:40,007 --> 00:00:42,476
JEROME: <i>I'm more
than a man, I'm an idea,</i>

21
00:00:42,543 --> 00:00:44,478
<i>and I will live on
in the shadows,</i>

22
00:00:44,545 --> 00:00:46,605
<i>within Gotham's discontent.</i>

23
00:00:51,118 --> 00:00:53,158
JEROME: <i>Burn it down, brother.</i>
(LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

24
00:01:04,431 --> 00:01:06,195
MAN: Brothers and sisters,

25
00:01:06,266 --> 00:01:08,758
let's raise a glass
to our fallen leader.

26
00:01:09,903 --> 00:01:10,903
To Jerome!

27
00:01:11,004 --> 00:01:12,905
ALL: To Jerome!

28
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:14,040
(GARGLING AND SPITTING)

29
00:01:16,176 --> 00:01:17,176
(ENGINE REVVING)

30
00:01:22,249 --> 00:01:23,249
(ENGINE STOPS)

31
00:01:30,157 --> 00:01:33,218
This affair is invitation only.

32
00:01:33,293 --> 00:01:34,293
(BELLS JINGLING)

33
00:01:37,731 --> 00:01:40,758
Well, that's all right,
you're welcome to stay.

34
00:01:40,867 --> 00:01:42,768
But you won't be leaving.

35
00:01:44,237 --> 00:01:46,763
(HORN HONKING LOUDLY)

36
00:01:52,779 --> 00:01:53,779
(INDISTINCT GROANING)

37
00:01:53,981 --> 00:01:56,473
JEROME: <i>Why so sad, bozos?</i>

38
00:01:56,583 --> 00:01:59,280
<i>Did you think they could
get rid of me so easily?</i>

39
00:02:00,087 --> 00:02:03,489
<i>Well, okay. So, they did.</i>

40
00:02:03,657 --> 00:02:06,559
<i>I'm dead, but let's
not dwell on negatives.</i>

41
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:09,494
<i>I have one last party to throw.</i>

42
00:02:09,596 --> 00:02:11,656
<i>- First on the to-do
list,</i> - (ALL LAUGHING)

43
00:02:12,265 --> 00:02:13,961
<i>dig me up.</i>

44
00:02:14,167 --> 00:02:15,601
<i>Dig me up!</i>

45
00:02:15,669 --> 00:02:16,830
MAN: You heard him!

46
00:02:17,270 --> 00:02:20,297
Come on, clowns! Dig him up!

47
00:02:20,374 --> 00:02:22,104
Get Jerome!

48
00:02:22,209 --> 00:02:25,043
We're gonna dig you
up, Jerome! You hear me?

49
00:02:25,545 --> 00:02:28,379
Come on out of there!
Come on, dig, dig, dig!

50
00:02:47,701 --> 00:02:51,331
- What are you gonna do?
- What can I do?

51
00:02:51,405 --> 00:02:54,807
The back door's just down
that hallway right there.

52
00:02:54,875 --> 00:02:58,744
- I'm not letting her go, Harvey.
- Why not?

53
00:02:58,845 --> 00:03:00,336
I'm the only one here.

54
00:03:00,414 --> 00:03:02,645
And I'm really good at
looking the other way, partner.

55
00:03:02,716 --> 00:03:03,716
Not this time.

56
00:03:04,051 --> 00:03:06,384
She robbed a dirty bank.

57
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:09,217
People get away with a lot
worse in Gotham every day.

58
00:03:09,322 --> 00:03:11,450
Doesn't make it right.

59
00:03:11,525 --> 00:03:15,018
We got away with
worse. Both of us.

60
00:03:15,662 --> 00:03:16,662
Get out of here.

61
00:03:16,830 --> 00:03:17,830
What?

62
00:03:17,898 --> 00:03:19,776
I don't need that crap
thrown in my face right now.

63
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:20,800
Get out of here!

64
00:03:27,007 --> 00:03:28,007
(DOOR OPENS)

65
00:03:34,781 --> 00:03:37,649
Well, you finally
nabbed me, copper.

66
00:03:40,887 --> 00:03:43,880
(SIGHS) What the hell, Lee?

67
00:03:44,024 --> 00:03:47,085
I don't suppose this is where
anyone expected our story to end.

68
00:03:48,361 --> 00:03:50,227
So, it's ending?

69
00:03:51,098 --> 00:03:53,533
Hard to imagine what's left.

70
00:03:55,902 --> 00:03:57,370
I wanna help you.

71
00:03:58,405 --> 00:04:01,068
- How?
- Give up Nygma.

72
00:04:01,141 --> 00:04:04,600
Return the money, and ask
the DA for supervised probation.

73
00:04:05,212 --> 00:04:06,373
I'm not betraying my friend.

74
00:04:07,881 --> 00:04:09,213
They can call you "the Doc,"

75
00:04:09,783 --> 00:04:12,582
you can rob banks, fight
gangsters, but I know you.

76
00:04:12,686 --> 00:04:16,123
You're Lee Thompkins.
And all this, this is just a...

77
00:04:17,424 --> 00:04:18,915
A way of helping people.

78
00:04:19,526 --> 00:04:21,017
I understand that.

79
00:04:21,094 --> 00:04:24,258
Who doesn't want to be Robin
Hood? But you're still breaking the law.

80
00:04:24,331 --> 00:04:26,596
Jim, you wish you
could do what I'm doing.

81
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:29,835
Helping people without
the straitjacket of the law?

82
00:04:30,003 --> 00:04:31,733
As if the law means
anything in Gotham.

83
00:04:31,805 --> 00:04:33,296
If the law has lost its meaning,

84
00:04:33,406 --> 00:04:35,618
it's because people like you
are turning your back on it.

85
00:04:35,642 --> 00:04:39,204
I am fighting back. I don't
deny anything I've done.

86
00:04:39,279 --> 00:04:40,923
You want to send me
to Blackgate? Go ahead.

87
00:04:40,947 --> 00:04:43,392
I don't want to send you to Blackgate!
It's the last thing I want to do!

88
00:04:43,416 --> 00:04:46,045
Don't you know I wish I
could let you walk out that door,

89
00:04:46,119 --> 00:04:48,452
- turn my head...
- What's holding you back?

90
00:04:48,588 --> 00:04:49,588
(EXHALES)

91
00:04:49,656 --> 00:04:53,320
Maybe if you'd let me go,
you'd let yourself go, too.

92
00:04:58,365 --> 00:05:02,132
There are so many things
I wish I could change.

93
00:05:02,202 --> 00:05:04,637
Things that I've done...

94
00:05:06,673 --> 00:05:07,936
Jim...

95
00:05:09,776 --> 00:05:10,776
(KNOCK AT DOOR)

96
00:05:14,981 --> 00:05:15,981
(DOOR OPENS)

97
00:05:16,483 --> 00:05:20,750
Sorry to stick my face in your
business, but something just came up.

98
00:05:20,854 --> 00:05:22,494
I've already inspected
it for booby traps.

99
00:05:23,590 --> 00:05:25,991
- It's clear.
- Well, that's a relief.

100
00:05:26,459 --> 00:05:29,293
I've taken the liberty of setting
up a monitor in your office.

101
00:05:33,867 --> 00:05:34,867
(ORGAN MUSIC PLAYING)

102
00:05:39,206 --> 00:05:41,675
You don't think he might
still be alive, do you?

103
00:05:41,775 --> 00:05:44,040
What were the
autopsy results, Lucius?

104
00:05:44,144 --> 00:05:46,943
Dead when he came in, more
dead when he was eviscerated,

105
00:05:47,013 --> 00:05:48,311
and his brain was sliced up.

106
00:05:48,381 --> 00:05:49,940
<i>Hello, Jimmy!</i>

107
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:51,951
<i>If you're watching this,</i>

108
00:05:52,018 --> 00:05:54,453
<i>things must not
have gone well for me.</i>

109
00:05:55,522 --> 00:05:57,081
<i>Shucks!</i> (CHUCKLES)

110
00:05:57,424 --> 00:06:00,485
<i>I can only pray, I
gave as good as I got,</i>

111
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:04,497
<i>and left ample
carnage in my wake.</i>

112
00:06:04,564 --> 00:06:07,033
<i>But I don't want to fixate
on disappointments.</i>

113
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:11,162
<i>Jimmy, I have one last
teensy request for you.</i>

114
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:14,970
<i>I want you to throw me a wake</i>

115
00:06:15,575 --> 00:06:18,010
<i>at the GCPD.</i>

116
00:06:18,311 --> 00:06:20,371
(AUDIO SCRAMBLING)
<i>Don't worry about the guest list.</i>

117
00:06:21,481 --> 00:06:24,508
<i>I've already sent
the invitations.</i>

118
00:06:24,684 --> 00:06:26,209
(LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

119
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:28,120
I don't like the sound of that.

120
00:06:28,288 --> 00:06:29,688
- (HORN HONKING)
- (PEOPLE SHOUTING)

121
00:06:38,899 --> 00:06:41,733
Is everybody ready?

122
00:06:41,868 --> 00:06:42,868
(MOB CHEERING)

123
00:06:45,772 --> 00:06:47,206
Lock down everything, now!

124
00:06:47,574 --> 00:06:51,341
Everybody listen up! Lock
it down! Lock it down, now!

125
00:06:56,182 --> 00:06:57,182
(CAR HORN HONKING)

126
00:07:11,765 --> 00:07:15,634
The Doc's taken care of us.
It's time for us to take care of her!

127
00:07:15,735 --> 00:07:17,246
Let's go down there,
and bust her out of jail.

128
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:19,215
No one cares about the fate of
Lee Thompkins more than me,

129
00:07:19,239 --> 00:07:20,239
is that understood?

130
00:07:20,573 --> 00:07:24,567
Which is exactly why I will not have
you bumbling into the GCPD en masse.

131
00:07:24,644 --> 00:07:26,078
So, we're going to let her rot?

132
00:07:26,479 --> 00:07:29,711
Leave her in the sweaty
palms of Jim Gordon?

133
00:07:29,783 --> 00:07:32,412
I would sooner debate you all
on teleology versus deontology,

134
00:07:32,485 --> 00:07:34,511
than leave her with that
overgrown Boy Scout.

135
00:07:34,621 --> 00:07:35,919
"Teleo..." Huh?

136
00:07:35,989 --> 00:07:36,989
My point exactly.

137
00:07:37,090 --> 00:07:38,820
Look, if I had it my way,

138
00:07:38,925 --> 00:07:41,451
Jim Gordon would be off the
field of play once and for all.

139
00:07:41,528 --> 00:07:44,157
But Lee insists that I
employ only nonlethal means.

140
00:07:44,264 --> 00:07:46,426
So, I and my
brilliant crack team

141
00:07:46,499 --> 00:07:48,991
will liberate Lee Thompkins
with surgical precision.

142
00:07:49,102 --> 00:07:50,102
You stay here.

143
00:07:50,170 --> 00:07:52,105
Team, we have everything?

144
00:07:52,172 --> 00:07:54,073
- Bicycle pump? Can opener?
- Right here.

145
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:57,770
Primer cord? Pickle
jar? Fishing rod?

146
00:07:57,844 --> 00:08:00,678
Fabulous. Okay, you
four, you're with me.

147
00:08:00,780 --> 00:08:02,976
You, go where Jim Gordon goes.

148
00:08:03,049 --> 00:08:05,450
He comes under
some harm, assist him.

149
00:08:05,518 --> 00:08:07,697
I do not need Lee blaming me
if he's killed under friendly fire,

150
00:08:07,721 --> 00:08:09,212
while I go about
my business, okay?

151
00:08:09,322 --> 00:08:10,847
All right, team, follow my plan,

152
00:08:10,957 --> 00:08:12,823
and we'll be back here
to finish counting this

153
00:08:12,892 --> 00:08:14,588
in just a few hours. Keep it up.

154
00:08:15,295 --> 00:08:17,628
Breaking Lee out is
going to be a piece of cake.

155
00:08:17,764 --> 00:08:18,764
(TELEPHONE RINGING)

156
00:08:19,432 --> 00:08:20,525
Hello, Wayne Manor.

157
00:08:20,633 --> 00:08:21,692
<i>Alfred, it's Gordon.</i>

158
00:08:21,801 --> 00:08:22,825
Where's Bruce?

159
00:08:22,936 --> 00:08:25,217
Well, he's meeting with
Jeremiah about the energy project.

160
00:08:25,271 --> 00:08:26,466
<i>Is something amiss?</i>

161
00:08:26,539 --> 00:08:28,030
He's meeting with
Jeremiah Valeska?

162
00:08:28,341 --> 00:08:29,341
Yes, that's right.

163
00:08:29,442 --> 00:08:31,934
Now, you can tell me why
you sound so concerned.

164
00:08:32,012 --> 00:08:34,379
Jerome's followers are
rampaging outside the station.

165
00:08:34,481 --> 00:08:35,481
Oh, I see.

166
00:08:35,548 --> 00:08:39,383
Are Master Bruce and
Jeremiah in any danger?

167
00:08:39,486 --> 00:08:41,079
It's hard to say. But right now,

168
00:08:41,187 --> 00:08:43,816
Jeremiah's maze may actually
be the safest place for him.

169
00:08:43,890 --> 00:08:47,486
Right, I shall head there
nonetheless. Thank you very much.

170
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:49,358
- (THUDDING)
- (PEOPLE SHOUTING)

171
00:09:00,573 --> 00:09:01,734
What's the plan?

172
00:09:02,442 --> 00:09:05,412
- Open up the armory.
- Now you're talkin'.

173
00:09:05,512 --> 00:09:06,512
Guys!

174
00:09:11,684 --> 00:09:12,684
(MAN LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

175
00:09:18,258 --> 00:09:20,557
- (GUNS COCKING)
- HARVEY: Jim! Hey, Jim!

176
00:09:20,660 --> 00:09:22,500
You figure out when
we're going to hit 'em yet?

177
00:09:22,896 --> 00:09:25,058
- We're not.
- Say what?

178
00:09:25,165 --> 00:09:26,497
You know how Jerome works,

179
00:09:26,599 --> 00:09:27,692
dead or alive.

180
00:09:27,767 --> 00:09:29,167
He uses distractions.

181
00:09:29,269 --> 00:09:30,346
So, what, we're
going to just let 'em

182
00:09:30,370 --> 00:09:31,914
come in through the
front door and party?

183
00:09:31,938 --> 00:09:34,169
This wake is just
intended to distract us,

184
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,751
while his followers
hit the real target.

185
00:09:35,775 --> 00:09:37,141
- Which is?
- Well,

186
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:38,354
we're never gonna
figure that out

187
00:09:38,378 --> 00:09:40,289
if we're inside, fighting
off these maniacs, are we?

188
00:09:40,313 --> 00:09:42,714
Look, they come in
the front door, right?

189
00:09:42,782 --> 00:09:45,274
You fall back, get a few
shots off, make it look good.

190
00:09:45,485 --> 00:09:46,953
Meanwhile, the entire precinct

191
00:09:47,053 --> 00:09:49,253
sneaks out this old service
door as quickly as possible.

192
00:09:49,622 --> 00:09:52,057
I can't believe you're going
to run away from these asses.

193
00:09:52,125 --> 00:09:54,720
Once we're outside, we
surround the building, cordon it off.

194
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:58,925
- And then we trap 'em all inside.
- Correct. They blow off some steam.

195
00:09:58,998 --> 00:10:01,092
We hit 'em with teargas,
and knock a few heads.

196
00:10:01,167 --> 00:10:03,261
Yeah. Of course, we
still have to figure out

197
00:10:03,336 --> 00:10:04,336
what the real target is.

198
00:10:04,437 --> 00:10:05,769
Got a plan for that?

199
00:10:05,839 --> 00:10:06,966
I do.

200
00:10:07,073 --> 00:10:10,237
It's a little sketchy
right now, but come on.

201
00:10:10,810 --> 00:10:12,540
All right, listen up, people!

202
00:10:13,646 --> 00:10:15,114
Here's the plan.

203
00:10:15,782 --> 00:10:17,751
Jeremiah,

204
00:10:17,817 --> 00:10:20,578
I didn't think you could get the
generator program working so quickly.

205
00:10:21,387 --> 00:10:22,587
You ready for a demonstration?

206
00:10:25,592 --> 00:10:27,151
Okay, you hit that switch there,

207
00:10:27,260 --> 00:10:30,628
and the facility will be
disconnected from the power grid.

208
00:10:38,471 --> 00:10:40,303
(GENERATOR POWERING UP)

209
00:10:48,648 --> 00:10:49,648
(ELECTRICITY BUZZING)

210
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:01,525
Ambient energy.

211
00:11:03,129 --> 00:11:07,999
No cables or wires of any
kind. It's clean and stable.

212
00:11:08,134 --> 00:11:11,161
Harvested from micro tremors
and air density shifts, it's...

213
00:11:11,804 --> 00:11:14,171
It's virtually without costs.

214
00:11:15,341 --> 00:11:19,335
And with the prototypes at Wayne
Labs, we can power all of Gotham?

215
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:23,047
You've kept this
project a secret, yes?

216
00:11:24,384 --> 00:11:27,013
No one outside of Wayne
Industries knows it exists.

217
00:11:28,855 --> 00:11:31,791
It's the ones who
are closest to you

218
00:11:31,858 --> 00:11:34,555
(WHISPERING) that you
have to keep your eye on.

219
00:11:35,628 --> 00:11:37,790
I know better than anyone.

220
00:11:40,733 --> 00:11:43,601
Arkham Asylum sent me
Jerome's personal effects,

221
00:11:43,703 --> 00:11:46,263
and amongst them,
I found his diary.

222
00:11:53,112 --> 00:11:55,513
It's a catalog of his
fantasies and goals.

223
00:11:55,582 --> 00:11:58,882
Every twisted
vision he ever had.

224
00:12:05,191 --> 00:12:07,558
Maybe you shouldn't spend
so much time reading it.

225
00:12:07,627 --> 00:12:11,826
He was obsessed with torturing and
murdering me, James Gordon, and you,

226
00:12:11,898 --> 00:12:13,890
and if he had been
just the least bit sane,

227
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:16,401
he would have destroyed us all.

228
00:12:17,937 --> 00:12:20,099
And Gotham would be in ruin.

229
00:12:24,877 --> 00:12:27,938
Your brother's dead, Jeremiah.

230
00:12:28,047 --> 00:12:31,575
It's time for you to come out of
this bunker and join the world.

231
00:12:32,952 --> 00:12:34,853
Yes.

232
00:12:35,888 --> 00:12:38,255
Yes, he's dead.

233
00:12:40,393 --> 00:12:43,454
- I still have trouble believing it.
- (PHONE VIBRATING)

234
00:12:44,731 --> 00:12:46,427
Who is that?

235
00:12:47,634 --> 00:12:48,932
It's just Alfred.

236
00:12:50,837 --> 00:12:51,837
Yeah?

237
00:12:51,938 --> 00:12:54,305
<i>Master Bruce, I've got
some rather disturbing news.</i>

238
00:12:54,741 --> 00:12:57,267
Jerome Valeska's acolytes
are kicking off again.

239
00:13:02,949 --> 00:13:03,949
Yes.

240
00:13:04,417 --> 00:13:08,013
<i>- Thank you, Alfred.</i>
- I'm on my way.

241
00:13:10,957 --> 00:13:12,653
Lunch plans.

242
00:13:15,261 --> 00:13:16,593
That was a lie.

243
00:13:20,266 --> 00:13:22,633
You're lying to me, Bruce?

244
00:13:24,804 --> 00:13:27,672
You're right. I'm sorry.

245
00:13:29,409 --> 00:13:33,608
It seems some of Jerome's
followers are causing trouble.

246
00:13:34,647 --> 00:13:39,483
Oh, my God. I was right.

247
00:13:40,086 --> 00:13:41,086
No, Jeremiah.

248
00:13:41,154 --> 00:13:43,851
I was right. He's not dead.

249
00:13:44,457 --> 00:13:47,222
Bruce, he's not dead. He's
alive, and he's coming after me!

250
00:13:50,963 --> 00:13:51,963
(GLASS SHATTERING)

251
00:14:10,249 --> 00:14:11,249
(GRUNTING AND SCREAMING)

252
00:14:14,087 --> 00:14:15,087
(GUNSHOTS)

253
00:14:18,791 --> 00:14:23,695
Jeremiah, easy, easy.
You're not thinking clearly.

254
00:14:23,796 --> 00:14:28,063
- Come on, this isn't like you.
- Bruce...

255
00:14:30,203 --> 00:14:32,365
Bruce, I need to
tell you something.

256
00:14:33,539 --> 00:14:37,340
After Jerome died, he left
one last final trap for me.

257
00:14:40,813 --> 00:14:43,715
He sprayed me
with his insanity gas.

258
00:14:44,851 --> 00:14:48,879
"It's a special mixture just
for you, brother," he said.

259
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:56,086
I can't stop seeing him.

260
00:14:58,898 --> 00:15:00,560
Clawing his way
out of his grave,

261
00:15:00,633 --> 00:15:03,467
coming for me, and even
though I know it's not real,

262
00:15:03,569 --> 00:15:06,198
it feels real.

263
00:15:08,641 --> 00:15:11,941
And I can't control myself.

264
00:15:12,745 --> 00:15:15,647
What if I could show
you he's dead and buried?

265
00:15:17,283 --> 00:15:18,342
How?

266
00:15:20,353 --> 00:15:23,551
- We go there, to his grave.
- No.

267
00:15:23,623 --> 00:15:25,421
- No, no, no.
- Jeremiah, listen to me.

268
00:15:25,525 --> 00:15:27,035
Your brother took away
your greatest strength,

269
00:15:27,059 --> 00:15:30,291
your mind, and
turned it into a trap.

270
00:15:30,463 --> 00:15:34,696
But if you can see the reality,
you can be freed from that trap.

271
00:15:40,039 --> 00:15:42,440
You really think
that would work?

272
00:15:44,043 --> 00:15:45,534
I do.

273
00:15:48,915 --> 00:15:50,611
Then I'll try.

274
00:15:52,618 --> 00:15:54,246
You're a good friend, Bruce.

275
00:16:00,993 --> 00:16:02,193
(PEOPLE GRUNTING AND SHOUTING)

276
00:16:06,833 --> 00:16:08,873
I'm getting you and the
other prisoners out of here.

277
00:16:09,001 --> 00:16:10,512
What were you trying
to tell me before, Jim?

278
00:16:10,536 --> 00:16:12,114
There's a van outside,
waiting for transfer.

279
00:16:12,138 --> 00:16:14,801
- Don't ignore me.
- I just want to get you safe first.

280
00:16:14,941 --> 00:16:16,671
- Come to The Narrows.
- What?

281
00:16:16,776 --> 00:16:18,736
Where you can make a
real difference in this city.

282
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:20,803
You can make up your
own rules about how to do it.

283
00:16:28,321 --> 00:16:29,321
(PEOPLE SHOUTING)

284
00:16:33,593 --> 00:16:34,593
(LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

285
00:16:35,962 --> 00:16:39,490
- Alvarez, get them out of here. Go.
- (ALARM BLARING)

286
00:16:42,168 --> 00:16:44,933
Don't shoot! Hold your fire.

287
00:16:45,972 --> 00:16:48,373
- (PEOPLE SHOUTING)
- (CHAINSAW WHIRRING)

288
00:17:01,721 --> 00:17:03,189
There's too many
of them. Fall back!

289
00:17:03,523 --> 00:17:05,355
Fall back!

290
00:17:05,491 --> 00:17:07,392
Fall back!

291
00:17:23,509 --> 00:17:24,636
Let's go! Let's go!

292
00:17:31,717 --> 00:17:32,717
(LAUGHING)

293
00:17:32,852 --> 00:17:34,343
Well, look at us.

294
00:17:35,321 --> 00:17:40,089
We caught ourselves
Captain James Gordon.

295
00:17:40,192 --> 00:17:43,026
Assassin of Jerome Valeska.

296
00:17:43,496 --> 00:17:44,496
Hi, guys.

297
00:17:44,597 --> 00:17:46,361
Don't try and get
chummy with us, Gordon.

298
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:48,866
We're gonna carve you up.

299
00:17:49,101 --> 00:17:52,071
Yeah, no, I wasn't talkin'
to you. I was talkin' to them.

300
00:17:52,772 --> 00:17:54,550
- Hey, man, you like to dance?
- (ELECTRICITY BUZZING)

301
00:17:54,574 --> 00:17:55,574
(FOLLOWERS GROANING)

302
00:17:59,378 --> 00:18:01,313
Let's you and me talk
outside, what do you say?

303
00:18:05,251 --> 00:18:06,411
(PHONE RINGING AND VIBRATING)

304
00:18:17,430 --> 00:18:18,430
(PHONE RINGING)

305
00:18:24,503 --> 00:18:26,543
- There's still no answer.
- Then something's wrong.

306
00:18:26,906 --> 00:18:29,034
- We should go.
- He was on his way to your office.

307
00:18:29,709 --> 00:18:31,268
He'll wait for us there.

308
00:18:33,412 --> 00:18:34,412
(TWIGS SNAPPING)

309
00:18:36,382 --> 00:18:37,873
What was that?

310
00:18:38,084 --> 00:18:39,552
(THUNDER CRACKING)

311
00:18:42,088 --> 00:18:45,616
We're almost there. Just a
quick look, and we'll leave.

312
00:18:47,793 --> 00:18:51,457
Bruce. Bruce.

313
00:18:54,133 --> 00:18:55,761
I don't know if I can do this.

314
00:18:57,703 --> 00:18:59,934
Just a little further.

315
00:19:12,318 --> 00:19:13,786
Oh, God, no.

316
00:19:13,853 --> 00:19:15,822
His followers must
have dug him up.

317
00:19:15,888 --> 00:19:17,652
He's still alive.

318
00:19:17,790 --> 00:19:18,883
I knew it.

319
00:19:18,991 --> 00:19:21,984
- We have to get out of here.
- I knew it.

320
00:19:22,128 --> 00:19:26,725
- He's alive!
- Jeremiah! Jeremiah!

321
00:19:42,515 --> 00:19:43,515
(BOTH GRUNTING)

322
00:19:45,785 --> 00:19:48,448
How much longer are these petty
aggressions going to continue?

323
00:19:48,521 --> 00:19:50,217
There's nothing petty
about my aggression.

324
00:19:50,790 --> 00:19:54,784
So, am I to starve until I guess
the source of your resentment?

325
00:19:57,329 --> 00:20:00,094
You said if I joined
you, we'd be back on top.

326
00:20:00,332 --> 00:20:03,996
Instead, we're grubbing for
Jerome, and we got played by Nygma.

327
00:20:04,603 --> 00:20:10,167
You said if I joined you,
you'd find me a cure. And, yet...

328
00:20:11,844 --> 00:20:16,839
I admit, that through
no fault of my own,

329
00:20:18,451 --> 00:20:20,545
our advancement
has not run apace.

330
00:20:20,619 --> 00:20:21,917
(SHOUTS) "Not run apace"?

331
00:20:22,254 --> 00:20:24,382
We're squatting in
Falcone's mansion.

332
00:20:24,523 --> 00:20:27,049
We're knockin' over liquor
stores to pay for groceries.

333
00:20:27,126 --> 00:20:30,563
Meanwhile, everyone else
is carving up Sofia's territory.

334
00:20:30,663 --> 00:20:33,155
We are lying in wait,
building a nest egg,

335
00:20:33,232 --> 00:20:36,498
while less deliberate
players show us their cards.

336
00:20:38,571 --> 00:20:42,008
If you don't find me Hugo
Strange and get me cured,

337
00:20:42,341 --> 00:20:45,038
I am going to crush your
windpipe like a beer can.

338
00:20:45,111 --> 00:20:46,111
Shh!

339
00:20:46,212 --> 00:20:50,081
- Did you just shush me?
- Shush! I sense an opportunity here.

340
00:20:50,182 --> 00:20:51,693
(REPORTER ON TV)
<i>live to Jennifer Glory.</i>

341
00:20:51,717 --> 00:20:54,346
<i>In a twist that Jerome Valeska
himself could've thought of,</i>

342
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:57,015
<i>the GCPD are laying
siege to Central Precinct,</i>

343
00:20:57,089 --> 00:21:00,890
<i>while Valeska's followers hold a
wake for their deceased role model.</i>

344
00:21:01,127 --> 00:21:02,891
How is that an opportunity?

345
00:21:02,962 --> 00:21:06,592
Confusion is always an
opportunity for the clearheaded.

346
00:21:06,665 --> 00:21:11,126
Someone is showing their
cards, Butch. Let's go take a peek.

347
00:21:13,072 --> 00:21:14,072
(GRUMBLES)

348
00:21:15,941 --> 00:21:16,941
(HELICOPTER HOVERING)

349
00:21:17,143 --> 00:21:18,143
(REPORTERS CHATTERING)

350
00:21:24,750 --> 00:21:27,618
One to the east, one
to the west. Let's go.

351
00:21:28,687 --> 00:21:31,282
- Is he talkin' yet?
- I don't know, let's check.

352
00:21:31,423 --> 00:21:33,085
MAN: Long live Jerome!

353
00:21:33,726 --> 00:21:35,456
HARVEY: All right.
One more time, sunshine.

354
00:21:35,561 --> 00:21:37,723
Did Jerome leave
any other instructions?

355
00:21:37,797 --> 00:21:39,095
- I'll never...
- (TASER BUZZING)

356
00:21:40,232 --> 00:21:43,634
Harvey! Harvey!
Reporters, buddy.

357
00:21:46,572 --> 00:21:48,372
All right, look, this is
how it's going to go.

358
00:21:49,108 --> 00:21:51,236
You're going to start talking,

359
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:53,745
or I'm gonna stop caring
whether you can talk, you got it?

360
00:21:53,813 --> 00:21:54,940
(MAN GROANING AND SCREAMING)

361
00:21:58,584 --> 00:21:59,584
I'll talk!

362
00:22:01,353 --> 00:22:04,016
It's too late, anyways.
They're already dead.

363
00:22:04,123 --> 00:22:05,318
Who? Who's dead?

364
00:22:06,025 --> 00:22:09,462
Jeremiah and Bruce Wayne.

365
00:22:10,830 --> 00:22:13,459
- You think he's tellin' the truth?
- I'm gonna find out.

366
00:22:13,532 --> 00:22:17,196
They're at Jeremiah's bunker.
You hold down the fort here?

367
00:22:17,570 --> 00:22:19,163
MAN: Long live Jerome!

368
00:22:19,238 --> 00:22:21,002
- (TASER BUZZING)
- (MAN SCREAMING)

369
00:22:25,644 --> 00:22:26,724
(SIREN BLARING IN DISTANCE)

370
00:22:29,715 --> 00:22:32,651
- Trouble, Mr. Riddler?
- A complication, yes.

371
00:22:33,552 --> 00:22:35,521
Hostiles take over the station.

372
00:22:36,522 --> 00:22:38,650
Police will remove the
prisoners. Where are they?

373
00:22:38,791 --> 00:22:39,791
(THUDDING)

374
00:22:42,795 --> 00:22:46,891
Oh, yes. This might be
easier than I expected.

375
00:22:47,233 --> 00:22:48,724
(LAUGHING)

376
00:22:52,004 --> 00:22:54,667
The Riddler! We're saved!

377
00:22:55,140 --> 00:22:56,506
How did you get out?

378
00:22:57,042 --> 00:22:58,408
Through the old service door.

379
00:23:01,413 --> 00:23:02,881
The old service door.

380
00:23:02,982 --> 00:23:05,349
- What do we do, now?
- Now we improvise.

381
00:23:05,417 --> 00:23:06,862
They're going to use
teargas in here soon.

382
00:23:06,886 --> 00:23:11,017
I have to get in first. We
need a costume shop. Quick!

383
00:23:14,793 --> 00:23:17,456
Penguin! We're saved!

384
00:23:18,464 --> 00:23:21,696
- That one.
- Jerome...

385
00:23:22,635 --> 00:23:23,635
No, not the trunk...

386
00:23:24,904 --> 00:23:27,601
You ever get tired
of being wrong?

387
00:23:41,754 --> 00:23:43,074
(PEOPLE SCREAMING
AND CHATTERING)

388
00:24:04,977 --> 00:24:05,977
(DOOR OPENING)

389
00:24:07,146 --> 00:24:08,671
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

390
00:24:13,252 --> 00:24:14,413
Jeremiah!

391
00:24:16,422 --> 00:24:18,789
We need to leave! It's not safe!

392
00:24:18,857 --> 00:24:20,849
JEREMIAH: You believe me now?

393
00:24:21,427 --> 00:24:23,020
Jerome's alive!

394
00:24:23,128 --> 00:24:26,428
No, his followers dug
him up. They're sick!

395
00:24:26,932 --> 00:24:30,494
They're also dangerous,
and they might be nearby!

396
00:24:30,602 --> 00:24:33,470
How can I trust you if
you won't believe me?

397
00:24:34,473 --> 00:24:37,443
You can trust me
because I'm your friend.

398
00:24:41,280 --> 00:24:45,342
I want you to be
my friend, Bruce.

399
00:24:45,517 --> 00:24:48,419
You don't know what it was like,

400
00:24:48,487 --> 00:24:52,982
living underground
all those years.

401
00:24:53,993 --> 00:24:57,953
Then you came along and offered
me everything I could dream of.

402
00:24:58,163 --> 00:25:01,133
Because I believe
in you, Jeremiah.

403
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:03,465
We're gonna do great
things for Gotham.

404
00:25:03,669 --> 00:25:08,437
We could. We really could.

405
00:25:09,675 --> 00:25:12,076
I thought we would.

406
00:25:12,177 --> 00:25:15,204
There's no reason
to stop thinking that.

407
00:25:15,314 --> 00:25:17,306
All we have to do,
is get out of here.

408
00:25:20,052 --> 00:25:24,990
First, all we had to do
was come to the cemetery.

409
00:25:26,692 --> 00:25:28,991
Now all we have to do is leave?

410
00:25:30,095 --> 00:25:31,723
See, that's very
confusing to me.

411
00:25:31,830 --> 00:25:36,530
So, tell me again, Bruce,

412
00:25:36,602 --> 00:25:39,162
why'd you really bring me here?

413
00:25:40,672 --> 00:25:42,334
I thought it would help.

414
00:25:42,408 --> 00:25:44,172
I was wrong. But
we need to leave.

415
00:25:44,543 --> 00:25:45,787
(SHOUTS) What the
hell are you doing?

416
00:25:45,811 --> 00:25:47,122
You think I didn't know
what was happening

417
00:25:47,146 --> 00:25:49,809
from the moment you
suggested coming here?

418
00:25:49,882 --> 00:25:54,149
- Jeremiah, what are you talking...
- Stop pretending to be my friend!

419
00:25:54,319 --> 00:25:56,015
I know what's really happening.

420
00:25:56,088 --> 00:26:02,324
You can fool everyone else,
but I know you made a switch.

421
00:26:02,394 --> 00:26:04,727
That, you can't hide.

422
00:26:04,863 --> 00:26:08,356
Not even behind
that new face of yours.

423
00:26:10,202 --> 00:26:12,933
I know it's you.

424
00:26:13,772 --> 00:26:16,037
I know it's you, Jerome.

425
00:26:16,575 --> 00:26:17,634
Jeremiah, give me the gun.

426
00:26:17,743 --> 00:26:18,743
(GUNSHOT)

427
00:26:21,613 --> 00:26:23,206
Turn around, brother.

428
00:26:25,150 --> 00:26:29,554
I said turn around! You
killed my friend Bruce.

429
00:26:30,589 --> 00:26:32,956
Now it's time to put
you back in your grave.

430
00:26:34,460 --> 00:26:35,553
Walk!

431
00:26:41,834 --> 00:26:43,154
(PEOPLE SCREAMING
AND CHATTERING)

432
00:26:56,582 --> 00:26:57,709
(STUTTERING)

433
00:27:05,057 --> 00:27:06,057
(LAUGHS NERVOUSLY)

434
00:27:23,342 --> 00:27:24,708
- (POT CLANGS)
- (GRUNTS)

435
00:27:26,612 --> 00:27:27,875
Ed!

436
00:27:29,181 --> 00:27:30,181
(DOOR OPENS)

437
00:27:37,289 --> 00:27:41,124
Bruce? Jeremiah?

438
00:28:05,450 --> 00:28:06,450
(STATIC BUZZING)

439
00:28:16,195 --> 00:28:19,688
Just a little bit further, brother.
Then you'll be back in your grave.

440
00:28:19,765 --> 00:28:21,859
You're stronger
than this, Jeremiah.

441
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:24,162
You know these ideas are
just the insanity gas talking.

442
00:28:24,236 --> 00:28:27,934
I won't let your lies
fool me any longer!

443
00:28:28,574 --> 00:28:29,574
(GASPING)

444
00:28:32,544 --> 00:28:33,773
What is happening?

445
00:28:37,583 --> 00:28:40,109
<i>- Hiya, Jimbo!</i>
- Jerome...

446
00:28:40,285 --> 00:28:41,285
<i>Ah!</i>

447
00:28:41,587 --> 00:28:43,419
<i>Don't bother talkin' to me.</i>

448
00:28:43,522 --> 00:28:48,688
<i>This is a recorded message,
and plus, I'm still dead.</i>

449
00:28:48,760 --> 00:28:50,695
<i>Just more posthumous fun.</i>

450
00:28:50,762 --> 00:28:55,598
<i>Look, I knew you'd see through
all those shenanigans at the station.</i>

451
00:28:55,901 --> 00:28:59,429
<i>I've given all my fans a
script for them to follow.</i>

452
00:29:00,372 --> 00:29:01,772
<i>See,</i>

453
00:29:02,574 --> 00:29:06,170
<i>I wanted to bring you here.</i>

454
00:29:06,245 --> 00:29:07,245
<i>Oh!</i>

455
00:29:09,615 --> 00:29:10,735
(JEROME LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

456
00:29:14,086 --> 00:29:15,884
Now do you believe
I'm not your brother?

457
00:29:19,358 --> 00:29:21,486
Jeremiah, listen to me!

458
00:29:21,660 --> 00:29:23,959
Jerome's followers
are doing this!

459
00:29:24,563 --> 00:29:26,122
Nothing else makes sense.

460
00:29:26,231 --> 00:29:30,168
He sent them
instructions to torment you.

461
00:29:30,269 --> 00:29:32,261
How fake.

462
00:29:32,337 --> 00:29:35,569
Yes, I can see quite clearly
where you cut off poor Bruce's face,

463
00:29:35,641 --> 00:29:36,939
and stitched on your own.

464
00:29:37,075 --> 00:29:40,773
But I am a man of science.

465
00:29:44,650 --> 00:29:46,744
So, let's have some
evidence, huh?

466
00:29:51,323 --> 00:29:52,323
<i>Oh!</i>

467
00:29:52,424 --> 00:29:53,915
<i>Don't mind her.</i>

468
00:29:53,992 --> 00:29:58,088
<i>She's just here to make sure
there's no talking during the movie.</i>

469
00:29:58,163 --> 00:30:01,565
<i>And, trust me, you're
gonna wanna pay attention,</i>

470
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:05,229
<i>so the twist makes
sense at the end.</i>

471
00:30:05,304 --> 00:30:06,304
(LAUGHS EVILLY)

472
00:30:06,772 --> 00:30:08,172
(CHOKING)

473
00:30:12,344 --> 00:30:13,344
(GORDON GRUNTING)

474
00:30:20,319 --> 00:30:24,120
Let's go, brother. Let's pull
off that grotesque facade.

475
00:30:24,323 --> 00:30:25,323
(JEREMIAH GRUNTING)

476
00:30:55,287 --> 00:30:56,380
Ecco.

477
00:30:56,488 --> 00:30:57,488
(JEROME CHOKING)

478
00:31:11,203 --> 00:31:14,230
<i>I tell you,</i>

479
00:31:14,373 --> 00:31:17,400
<i>suicide really takes it out
of a guy.</i> (CHUCKLING)

480
00:31:23,482 --> 00:31:25,747
<i>What is this?</i>

481
00:31:36,194 --> 00:31:39,961
Jeremiah! Do not let
him turn you into him!

482
00:31:41,066 --> 00:31:44,730
- Do not let Jerome win this battle!
- (JEROME STRAINING)

483
00:31:44,803 --> 00:31:47,466
Jerome, beat me?
That'll be the day.

484
00:31:48,774 --> 00:31:49,969
No!

485
00:31:50,142 --> 00:31:51,142
(JEREMIAH LAUGHING)

486
00:31:53,779 --> 00:31:55,111
Long live Jerome!

487
00:31:55,414 --> 00:31:57,178
- Long live Jerome!
- Long live Jerome!

488
00:31:57,249 --> 00:31:59,184
- Long live Jerome!
- Long live Jerome!

489
00:31:59,384 --> 00:32:01,512
Jerome is victorious at last!

490
00:32:11,563 --> 00:32:13,930
Jerome victorious?

491
00:32:17,068 --> 00:32:18,764
Are you serious?

492
00:32:20,539 --> 00:32:22,269
He's dead.

493
00:32:22,441 --> 00:32:25,934
Haven't you been
paying attention?

494
00:32:38,290 --> 00:32:40,452
JEREMIAH: <i>Thank
God I'm done with that.</i>

495
00:32:55,941 --> 00:32:58,911
I am the one who's victorious.

496
00:33:01,480 --> 00:33:02,812
<i>Jerome is dead.</i>

497
00:33:03,248 --> 00:33:04,409
(ECHOING) <i>Is dead... Is dead.</i>

498
00:33:05,183 --> 00:33:06,913
<i>Long live... Long live me.</i>

499
00:33:08,854 --> 00:33:11,414
<i>Long live me.</i>

500
00:33:20,499 --> 00:33:22,468
Look, Bruce,

501
00:33:24,302 --> 00:33:28,797
like everything Jerome set his
mind to, his insanity gas failed.

502
00:33:28,874 --> 00:33:32,970
Other than some
mild cosmetic effects,

503
00:33:33,044 --> 00:33:36,037
he might as well have
sprayed me with water.

504
00:33:36,481 --> 00:33:39,974
You all need to see Jerome
for the utter dud that he was.

505
00:33:40,051 --> 00:33:44,045
So, I donned the mask of madness

506
00:33:44,155 --> 00:33:49,992
to show you how feeble that is
compared to actual greatness.

507
00:33:52,364 --> 00:33:57,701
Behold, the face of true sanity.

508
00:33:57,769 --> 00:34:01,171
But looks aren't everything.

509
00:34:01,506 --> 00:34:06,376
I have a compendium of
Jerome's obsessions and goals.

510
00:34:07,812 --> 00:34:10,077
I will outdo every one of them.

511
00:34:11,416 --> 00:34:16,320
Jerome wanted to turn
Gotham into a madhouse.

512
00:34:17,188 --> 00:34:20,215
But to truly build something,

513
00:34:21,192 --> 00:34:24,754
you must first tear down
what is already there.

514
00:34:25,664 --> 00:34:28,395
JEREMIAH: <i>I apologize
for the deception, Jim.</i>

515
00:34:28,500 --> 00:34:30,093
<i>I needed to ape Jerome</i>

516
00:34:30,201 --> 00:34:32,102
<i>in order to persuade
his followers to throw that</i>

517
00:34:32,203 --> 00:34:34,900
<i>macabre celebration
at your police station.</i>

518
00:34:36,374 --> 00:34:40,778
<i>They are a pathetic lot,
but not without their uses.</i>

519
00:34:42,614 --> 00:34:43,614
(DOOR LOCKING)

520
00:34:44,482 --> 00:34:48,943
<i>Sidebar, that is a
self-perpetuating generator.</i>

521
00:34:49,054 --> 00:34:52,456
<i>It can store a phenomenal
amount of energy.</i>

522
00:34:52,958 --> 00:34:57,453
<i>I would hate to be within a
mile of it if it were to overload.</i>

523
00:35:01,666 --> 00:35:03,134
BRUCE: <i>Jeremiah, the gas worked.</i>

524
00:35:03,802 --> 00:35:08,638
Think about it. You want to carry
out Jerome's crazy plans sanely?

525
00:35:08,740 --> 00:35:11,471
- What could be madder than that?
- "Madder"?

526
00:35:12,310 --> 00:35:13,778
Let's see.

527
00:35:14,479 --> 00:35:16,072
Ah, here, for example.

528
00:35:16,982 --> 00:35:19,144
Jerome wanted to
slather you in honey,

529
00:35:19,250 --> 00:35:22,379
and have you eaten
alive by corpse beetles.

530
00:35:23,388 --> 00:35:24,913
Now, that's mad.

531
00:35:25,624 --> 00:35:28,059
Me, if I wanna kill
you, I'll just do it.

532
00:35:28,727 --> 00:35:31,595
I'll shoot you in the
head. (COCKING GUN)

533
00:35:31,663 --> 00:35:34,326
Simply and sanely.

534
00:35:35,166 --> 00:35:36,691
- (FOLLOWERS TITTERING)
- Jeremiah...

535
00:35:37,869 --> 00:35:39,838
But I don't want to kill you.

536
00:35:40,105 --> 00:35:41,105
(FOLLOWERS GROANING)

537
00:35:42,874 --> 00:35:46,811
Are you gonna listen, or are
you gonna behave like children?

538
00:35:47,379 --> 00:35:51,680
See, I don't want to kill you,
because I wanna show you

539
00:35:51,783 --> 00:35:53,684
how much I've changed things.

540
00:35:54,119 --> 00:35:56,679
How much we've changed things.

541
00:35:56,788 --> 00:35:58,984
Because I could not
have done any of this

542
00:36:00,392 --> 00:36:03,123
without your help.

543
00:36:04,529 --> 00:36:05,792
My help?

544
00:36:06,698 --> 00:36:08,326
JEREMIAH: <i>That
sound you are hearing,</i>

545
00:36:08,700 --> 00:36:09,700
(GENERATOR BUZZING)

546
00:36:10,368 --> 00:36:12,928
<i>that is a very bad sound.</i>

547
00:36:14,939 --> 00:36:16,703
<i>One which, I'm afraid,</i>

548
00:36:17,175 --> 00:36:20,145
<i>makes you something
of a guinea pig, Jim.</i>

549
00:36:20,612 --> 00:36:22,372
JEREMIAH: <i>I feel very
indebted to you, Bruce.</i>

550
00:36:23,314 --> 00:36:28,218
See, those generators that
we built with your money,

551
00:36:28,887 --> 00:36:30,856
they work even better as bombs.

552
00:36:30,989 --> 00:36:32,184
(BEEPING)

553
00:36:32,290 --> 00:36:35,351
<i>Killing you will help secure
the loyalty of Jerome's minions.</i>

554
00:36:35,460 --> 00:36:37,395
<i>And, well...</i>

555
00:36:38,096 --> 00:36:39,564
<i>That is that.</i>

556
00:36:42,033 --> 00:36:43,433
<i>Goodbye.</i>

557
00:36:43,535 --> 00:36:46,664
All right, everybody, listen
up! You know what to do!

558
00:36:46,738 --> 00:36:48,730
Let's go get our house back!

559
00:36:50,175 --> 00:36:51,175
(DISTANT EXPLOSION)

560
00:36:52,277 --> 00:36:53,277
(ALARM BLARING)

561
00:37:13,565 --> 00:37:15,261
That's one down.

562
00:37:16,367 --> 00:37:18,087
- Jim Gordon is dead.
- (FOLLOWERS CHEERING)

563
00:37:18,570 --> 00:37:21,540
- No! No!
- Yes, Bruce.

564
00:37:22,040 --> 00:37:25,442
Sorry, but progress
requires sacrifice.

565
00:37:25,777 --> 00:37:27,211
I'm going to stop you.

566
00:37:27,278 --> 00:37:32,080
I really hope you don't try. I
would hate to have to kill you.

567
00:37:32,851 --> 00:37:35,946
In fact, I can honestly say,

568
00:37:38,423 --> 00:37:41,154
you are my very best friend.

569
00:38:07,585 --> 00:38:09,417
What I want to know,

570
00:38:09,487 --> 00:38:12,821
with a minimum of fuss,

571
00:38:12,924 --> 00:38:17,294
is what you and your cohort
were really up to today?

572
00:38:19,297 --> 00:38:21,232
I'll never betray
the memory of...

573
00:38:22,667 --> 00:38:24,101
Wouldn't dream of it.

574
00:38:24,169 --> 00:38:28,971
I don't expect you to betray
the memory of that old corpse.

575
00:38:29,073 --> 00:38:34,239
I want you to betray whomever
it is you are currently following.

576
00:38:36,981 --> 00:38:39,974
- Long live Jerome.
- He's not talking.

577
00:38:40,084 --> 00:38:41,279
Is that so?

578
00:38:44,322 --> 00:38:45,449
You starin' at me?

579
00:38:48,226 --> 00:38:50,627
Yeah, I get it.

580
00:38:51,396 --> 00:38:56,801
Sometimes, I accidentally catch
a glimpse of myself in the mirror.

581
00:38:56,868 --> 00:39:00,964
It scares me, too.
And then I get angry.

582
00:39:02,740 --> 00:39:07,906
The longer I'm like
this, the angrier I get.

583
00:39:08,246 --> 00:39:11,944
And right now, the way I see it,

584
00:39:12,016 --> 00:39:15,509
you are preventing
me from finding a cure.

585
00:39:17,522 --> 00:39:18,888
And that

586
00:39:18,990 --> 00:39:24,054
makes me very, very angry.

587
00:39:24,162 --> 00:39:30,159
Is your plan to gain his sympathy
by reciting your tale of woe?

588
00:39:31,002 --> 00:39:35,406
Nah. Just wanted to see if I could get
him to pee his pants a little in terror.

589
00:39:36,708 --> 00:39:39,872
You want me to shove some chicken
bones up his nose till he squawks?

590
00:39:40,478 --> 00:39:43,607
- Yes, that will do.
- No.

591
00:39:44,182 --> 00:39:45,411
Let's make this quick.

592
00:39:45,683 --> 00:39:46,683
(STRAINING)

593
00:39:46,751 --> 00:39:48,185
- Tilt your head back.
- No!

594
00:39:48,253 --> 00:39:51,223
- Here comes the wishbone train!
- No, no! (SCREAMING)

595
00:39:55,927 --> 00:40:00,388
Smartest man in Gotham, and
you let your heart do the thinking.

596
00:40:01,199 --> 00:40:02,428
Wake up, Ed!

597
00:40:02,700 --> 00:40:03,700
Ow!

598
00:40:04,402 --> 00:40:07,270
- Were you awake the whole time?
- Maybe.

599
00:40:07,805 --> 00:40:09,273
"The smartest man
in Gotham," huh?

600
00:40:09,374 --> 00:40:12,572
All right, get up. Up, up, up.

601
00:40:12,644 --> 00:40:14,510
There are better things
to aspire to, you know.

602
00:40:15,914 --> 00:40:18,941
I'm aspiring to them
very much. (BLOWS)

603
00:40:19,284 --> 00:40:21,219
Just be yourself.

604
00:40:21,552 --> 00:40:24,044
The guy who can let go
of the past and change,

605
00:40:24,589 --> 00:40:26,023
I like that guy.

606
00:40:27,191 --> 00:40:29,036
All right, now, how are we
going to get past these psychos?

607
00:40:29,060 --> 00:40:30,771
I'm assuming you brought
one of those for me?

608
00:40:30,795 --> 00:40:33,788
No. I'd be into that,
but they only had one.

609
00:40:34,032 --> 00:40:35,261
Instead...

610
00:40:37,101 --> 00:40:40,538
- The cavalry should be coming very soon.
- Great.

611
00:40:41,072 --> 00:40:43,132
- (ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)
- (PEOPLE CHATTERING)

612
00:40:48,780 --> 00:40:50,681
(TEAR GAS SHELLS HISSING)

613
00:40:53,117 --> 00:40:55,109
(PEOPLE SHOUTING AND COUGHING)

614
00:41:02,327 --> 00:41:04,319
- Round them up!
- (GUNS COCKING)

615
00:41:14,973 --> 00:41:17,169
Move, move, move! Let's go!

616
00:41:27,852 --> 00:41:28,852
Okay.

617
00:41:37,795 --> 00:41:39,855
Don't just wrap me
around your finger, Lee.

618
00:41:40,965 --> 00:41:42,593
Come on, let's run.

619
00:41:45,703 --> 00:41:46,703
(GRUNTS)

620
00:41:47,138 --> 00:41:49,573
That's for takin' a
leak on my desk.

621
00:41:53,978 --> 00:41:55,344
What a mess.

622
00:41:55,413 --> 00:41:56,413
You know, it's funny,

623
00:41:56,514 --> 00:41:59,313
it kind of reminds me of my
first apartment in Crown Point.

624
00:41:59,417 --> 00:42:00,476
How long ago was that?

625
00:42:01,152 --> 00:42:03,712
- I still live there.
- GORDON: Harvey.

626
00:42:04,222 --> 00:42:06,054
I found the epicenter
of that explosion.

627
00:42:07,725 --> 00:42:09,318
It's Jeremiah's bunker.

628
00:42:09,660 --> 00:42:11,526
That's where Jim was
going to look for Bruce.

629
00:42:18,236 --> 00:42:21,468
- Good evening, gentlemen.
- Hey there, Mr. Valeska.

630
00:42:22,507 --> 00:42:24,976
You alone, or you got
Mr. Wayne with you?

631
00:42:25,043 --> 00:42:26,477
No Mr. Wayne.

632
00:42:29,414 --> 00:42:30,882
But I'm not alone.

633
00:42:35,686 --> 00:42:36,686
What the...

634
00:42:59,577 --> 00:43:05,039
Look at these. The
gifts of true friendship.

635
00:43:06,284 --> 00:43:08,879
Let's load them on the trucks.

636
00:43:10,154 --> 00:43:13,591
It's time to give Gotham
City its new face.
